{
  "id": "somatotopic-organization",
  "term": "somatotopic organization",
  "definition": "Somatotopic organization is a patterned brain mapping in which seeing or using a particular body part is linked to activity in the corresponding sensorimotor area for that body part. In this context, it refers to the matching of observed hand or foot actions with hand- or foot-related regions of the observer’s brain.",
